\begin_layout Proof
Tending 
\begin_inset Formula $T_{n}$
\end_inset

 to infinity then will fill the integers from 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

 to 
\begin_inset Formula $\infty$
\end_inset

.
 If any other cycle (not ending by 1) existed, it would lead to an infinite
 number of values breaking the counting function 
\begin_inset Formula $N_{i}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

